 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "How do you break a wall that stood for a thousand years?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "With the biggest cannon the world had ever seen. This is Istanbul, today Türkiye's largest city."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Are the old walls still standing?",
   "scene": "today",
   "date": "Today",
   "place": "Istanbul"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Most of them, yes. Five point seven kilometres of land walls, from the Golden Horn to the Sea of Marmara, built in the early four hundreds."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "First a moat twenty metres wide. Then an outer wall, then an inner wall twelve metres high, with ninety-six towers.",
   "scene": "heights",
   "date": "",
   "say": "First a moat twenty metres wide. Then an outer wall, then an inner wall twelve metres high, with ninety-six towers."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And no one ever got through?",
   "scene": "walls",
   "date": "1836",
   "place": "Theodosian Walls",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.45,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "For about a thousand years, no army broke through these land walls."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So what was left of Byzantium by then?",
   "scene": "lands1451",
   "date": "1451",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Almost nothing. The city itself, and the Morea in southern Greece. The Ottomans held everything around it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "That year a new sultan took the throne: Mehmed the Second. And he wanted the city.",
   "scene": "mehmed",
   "date": "1451",
   "place": "Edirne",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.38,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "First, he built a fortress on the Bosphorus in just a few months, to cut the city off from the Black Sea.",
   "scene": "bosphorus",
   "date": "1452",
   "place": "Bosphorus"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "It still stands today: Rumeli Hisarı.",
   "scene": "rumeli",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.45,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.4,
     0.35,
     1.3
    ]
   },
   "say": "It still stands today: Roo-meh-lee His-sar."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "But how do you get through walls like that?",
   "scene": "gun"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "That's where Orban comes in, a Hungarian cannon maker. He first offered his guns to the Byzantine emperor, who could not pay him."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "So he went to Mehmed, and built a bronze giant about eight metres long, firing stone balls of around two hundred and seventy kilos."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How often could it fire?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Only a few times a day. Reloading took about three hours."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "When did the siege begin?",
   "scene": "siege",
   "date": "6 April 1453",
   "place": "Constantinople",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.6,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "On the sixth of April, 1453. Mehmed was just twenty-one."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "He brought up to eighty thousand soldiers.",
   "scene": "armies"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Emperor Constantine the Eleventh had about seven thousand defenders.",
   "scene": "constantine",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.45,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The guns pounded the walls day after day. But every night, the defenders rebuilt the damage.",
   "scene": "siegemap",
   "date": "April 1453",
   "place": "Constantinople"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "And a great chain across the Golden Horn kept the Ottoman fleet out of the harbour."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "So the walls were holding?",
   "scene": "lands1453",
   "date": "April 1453",
   "place": "Ottoman lands"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "They were. Mehmed needed another way in. Next time: the fleet that crossed a hill. Like the video and follow History Sketches."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: ships over the hill",
   "sub": "Follow History Sketches"
  }
 ]
